01:05:09,230 --> 01:05:15,230
Superman Returns is a 2006 American superhero film
based on the DC Comics character Superman.

12
01:11:04,615 --> 01:11:10,615
The film was directed by Bryan Singer, and written by Michael Dougherty and
Dan Harris from a story by Singer, Dougherty and Harris.

13
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
It serves as an homage sequel to Superman (1978) and Superman II (1980), ignoring the events of
Superman III (1983), Supergirl (1984), and Superman IV: The Quest for Peace (1987).

14
01:22:55,384 --> 01:23:01,384
The film stars Brandon Routh as Superman, Kate Bosworth as Lois Lane and Kevin Spacey as Lex Luthor,
with James Marsden, Frank Langella, Eva Marie Saint and Parker Posey in supporting roles.

15
01:28:50,769 --> 01:28:56,769
In the film, Superman returns to Earth after five years and discovers that his love interest Lois Lane has moved
on from him and that his archenemy Lex Luthor is planning to kill him and reshape North America.

16
01:34:46,153 --> 01:34:52,153
After a series of unsuccessful projects to resurrect Superman following the
critical and financial failure of The Quest for Peace, Warner Bros.

17
01:40:41,538 --> 01:40:47,538
Pictures hired Singer to direct Superman Returns in July 2004.

18
01:46:36,923 --> 01:46:42,923
The majority of principal photography took place at Fox Studios Australia, Sydney while the visual effects sequences were handled by a number of studios, including Sony
Pictures Imageworks, Rhythm & Hues Studios (R&H), Framestore CFC, Rising Sun Pictures and The Orphanage; filming began in March 2005 and ended in November.

19
01:52:32,307 --> 01:52:38,307
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised its visual effects,
storyline and Singer's direction, but criticized its screenplay and runtime.

20
01:58:27,692 --> 01:58:33,692
While the film was one of the biggest films of the year, earning $391.1 million on a budget of
$204–223 million and becoming the ninth highest-grossing film of 2006, Warner Bros.

21
02:04:23,076 --> 02:04:29,076
was disappointed with the worldwide box office return and
cancelled a sequel for release in 2009.

22
02:10:18,461 --> 02:10:24,461
The Superman film series was rebooted in 2013 with Man of Steel,
directed by Zack Snyder and starring Henry Cavill as Superman.

23
02:16:13,846 --> 02:16:19,846
Routh later reprised his role as Superman in the 2019
Arrowverse crossover "Crisis on Infinite Earths".

24
02:22:09,230 --> 02:22:15,230
The film explores themes of saving the world, superhero,
invulnerability, based on comic, sequel.

25
02:28:04,615 --> 02:28:10,615
The tone is thought_provoking.
